    {
      "id": "starter.stop.stop-then-yield",
      "ruleIds": ["stop-before-stop-line"],
      "paragraphs": [
        "The STOP sign and the single continuous white line mean a complete stop, close to and before the line, with the front of the car behind it.",
        "Stopping does not give you priority. After the stop, give way to traffic from the right and the left, then move off when it is safe."
      ],
      "termIds": ["stop-sign", "stop-line"],
      "sourceRefs": [
        {
          "sourceId": "spf-btt-2026",
          "pdfPage": 11,
          "printedPage": "10",
