          "pdfPage": 53,
          "printedPage": "52",
          "drawing": null,
          "drawingRevision": null,
          "bboxPdfPoints": null,
          "section": "§81 The 'Give Way' Rule At Road Junctions",
          "quote": "Where there is a “STOP” sign, stop before the stop-line."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "starter.stop.close-to-and-before-line",
      "ruleIds": ["stop-before-stop-line"],
      "paragraphs": [
        "The handbook says stop close to and before the line. Both halves matter: not over the line, and not far back on the approach.",
        "Your front must stay behind the line. Stopping with the wheels on the line, or well before the sign, is not a stop at the line."
      ],
      "termIds": ["stop-line", "stop-sign"],
      "sourceRefs": [
        {
          "sourceId": "spf-btt-2026",
          "pdfPage": 36,
          "printedPage": "35",
          "drawing": null,
          "drawingRevision": null,
          "bboxPdfPoints": null,
          "section": "§52(b) Single White Line",
          "quote": "Horizontal white line indicates that traffic is required to stop and must stop close to and before this line."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "starter.stop.not-a-give-way",
      "ruleIds": ["stop-before-stop-line", "give-way-at-double-broken-line"],
      "paragraphs": [
        "Slowing and rolling through when the road looks clear is what a Give Way line allows; the comparison scene shows this access with that control instead.",
        "A STOP sign with a single continuous line means stop every time, even when nothing is coming."
      ],
      "termIds": ["stop-line", "stop-sign", "give-way-line"],
